 }}" id="text-2ba929df81" class="cmp-text" data-external-icon="true"> About Workfare Introduced in 2007, WIS supplements the incomes and CPF savings of lower-income workers to help them save for retirement. Workfare is targeted at Singaporean workers whose earnings are in the bottom 20%, with some support for those slightly above. Over S$12.9 billion 1 of WIS has been disbursed to 1.13 million 1 lower-income workers. 1 As at February 2026, up to WY2025 2 WIS 2 Work Year (WY) refers to the calendar year of work done. View more Workfare is paid in the form of CPF payments and cash to supplement their incomes. Employee WIS for employees If you are an eligible employee, you will receive CPF payments to help you save for retirement, plus cash payments to supplement your income. span style=\ font-weight: normal;\ >Eligibility /span> /div>
